From 146a7968eee149351f3694ea0859badd0bbb5558 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel FORTE <2580288+g4bwy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:55:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] [Model Loader][Qwen4Exp] Gather file-backed PLE rows
 through a persistent mmap

host_file_gather serves each step's PLE rows with one preadv syscall per
distinct row. That re-derives, 32k times per prefill step, a page the kernel
already has mapped for this process: the fd, page-cache lookup, kmap and fput
cost more than the 2 KB copy they perform. Measured on the 4x170HX box, the
per-row loop is the batch-prefill bottleneck; GPU0 (the PLE rank) tops out near
90% because the CPU gather sits on the critical path behind the whole-stream
sync.

Add an opt-in gather backend, `--engram-config '{"host_file_gather": true,
"host_file_gather_mmap": true}'`. At bind, map each checkpoint shard file once
read-only and view its table rows as tensors. Each step then gathers with one
batched `index_select` per shard instead of a preadv loop: warm rows become
plain loads of resident pages. The `POSIX_FADV_WILLNEED` pre-queue stays, so
cold pages are still fetched coalesced rather than faulted one at a time - the
failure mode that made the earlier mmap backend (PR #54129) slower on cold
starts.

The trade is the property preadv exists for. Mapped pages live in the worker's
address space for the process lifetime and are reclaimed only by unmapping, so
this is for hosts where the table fits in the page cache anyway and prefill
throughput matters; the default preadv path is unchanged for memory-tight
boxes. Chosen per-deployment, not automatic.

Scatter gather on a 32k-row step measured ~30 ms (preadv) -> ~3 ms (mmap),
byte-identical rows. CPU tests: new backend-selection and mmap/preadv
equivalence cases pass; test_ple, test_config, test_envs and the drop_cache
loader suite match baseline. Hardware trial pending: boot both modes, compare
GPU0 utilization, cold 1M, 100/4 wall, and confirm byte-exact rows on FP8.
